{
  "window_id": "w0023",
  "observed_failures": [
    {
      "filename": "078.jpg",
      "field": "total_amount",
      "observed": "\"\" (empty string)",
      "evidence": "Receipt shows 'Total Inclusive GST: 10.40'; feedback marks amount_correct=false; delivered cell is empty string, not a real null.",
      "failure_mode": "format_contract_violation: empty string written where a null was required"
    },
    {
      "filename": "077.jpg",
      "field": "total_amount",
      "observed": "23.26",
      "evidence": "Receipt has two tier-equivalent lines: 'Total (Inclusive of GST): 23.26' followed by 'Rounding Adj: -0.01' then final 'TOTAL: 23.25'. Predictor picked the earlier Total rather than the final one.",
      "failure_mode": "wrong_candidate_selection: did not prefer the last/rounded final TOTAL within the same priority tier"
    },
    {
      "filename": "074.jpg",
      "field": "total_amount",
      "observed": "702.00",
      "evidence": "Thai Delicious receipt shows 'Total: 92.80', 'Grand Total: 92.80', 'Cash Received: 100.00', 'Change: 7.20'. Predicted 702.00 has no source in the text and almost certainly came from an OCR hallucination or merged tokens on a single pass.",
      "failure_mode": "single_pass_ocr_noise: no multi-variant voting / sanity check; a garbled number was accepted"
    },
    {
      "filename": "034.jpg",
      "field": "date",
      "observed": "2018-08-09",
      "evidence": "Receipt label reads 'Date: 09/03/2018'. Predictor produced 2018-08-09, i.e. it parsed a different date string (likely a noisy or unrelated date token) instead of the labeled Date line, or mis-ordered day/month.",
      "failure_mode": "wrong_date_candidate: no preference for date tokens adjacent to a 'Date' label; day/month locale not anchored"
    },
    {
      "scope": "run_control",
      "evidence": "execution_metadata.termination_reason='max_iterations' at 65; stop_reason='max_iterations'; n_skill_invocations=0 (skills were preloaded but the invoke_skill tool was never called).",
      "failure_mode": "budget_exhaustion_before_convergence: agent iterated on ad-hoc OCR tweaks per image rather than consolidating into the skill-driven pipeline"
    }
  ],
  "root_causes": [
    "image-ocr skill's receipt field extractor leaves the 'pick among same-tier candidates' rule ambiguous: current draft uses first match within a tier, but final totals on Malaysian receipts often appear AFTER a rounding-adjustment line; the extractor must prefer the LAST same-tier match below any 'Rounding Adj'/'Total After Rounding' line, not the first.",
    "image-ocr skill recommends multi-pass OCR but does not require voting/consensus or sanity bounds on extracted numbers; a single corrupt pass can produce impossible values (e.g. 702.00 when all visible totals are ~92.80).",
    "image-ocr skill's date extractor iterates DATE_PATTERNS in a fixed list order and returns the first regex hit anywhere in the text, with no preference for a date that appears on a line containing a 'Date'/'Tarikh'/'Invoice Date' label; it also has no tie-break when both %d/%m/%Y and %m/%d/%Y could parse.",
    "xlsx skill describes null-vs-empty handling but the per-image pipeline example returns strings and the writing example does not force None/pd.NA conversion before to_excel; the agent produced an empty string for 078 instead of a true null cell.",
    "No skill instructs the agent to cap work-per-image and fall through to null when confidence is low, so the agent burned the 65-iteration budget debugging individual images instead of hardening the shared pipeline."
  ],
  "skill_defects": [
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "defect": "extract_total chooses first same-tier match; needs explicit 'prefer the last same-tier candidate, and if a 'Rounding Adj'/'Total After Rounding'/'Rounded Total' line exists, prefer the total that follows it' rule."
    },
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "defect": "No consensus/voting procedure across OCR variants, and no sanity filter (e.g., reject totals that differ by >5x from any other same-tier candidate across variants, or that exceed a reasonable receipt bound)."
    },
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "defect": "extract_date has no label-proximity preference and no locale hint. Should: (1) first scan lines containing 'Date'/'Tarikh'/'Invoice Date'/'Inv Date' and extract from those; (2) default to day-first (DD/MM) for ambiguous numeric dates typical of Malaysian/SG/UK receipts; (3) reject dates outside a plausible window."
    },
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "defect": "No per-image iteration budget or 'return (None, None) on low confidence' guidance; encourages open-ended retries that can exhaust the agent loop."
    },
    {
      "skill": "xlsx",
      "defect": "Strict-schema section shows the pattern but does not forbid writing '' for missing values nor require a final normalization pass that converts '', 'nan', 'None', NaN → None before to_excel. The 078 failure traces directly to this gap."
    },
    {
      "skill": "xlsx",
      "defect": "Verification checklist does not include an assertion that empty/missing cells read back as NaN/None (not the string 'nan' or ''); needs an explicit post-write check."
    }
  ],
  "repair_recommendations": [
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "change": "In the Structured Field Extraction section, replace the 'try candidates from first match' behavior with: within a tier, collect all non-excluded matches; if the text contains a 'ROUNDING ADJ', 'TOTAL AFTER ROUNDING', or 'ROUNDED TOTAL' line, prefer the last match that appears at or after that line; otherwise prefer the last match in reading order. Document this rule explicitly with a worked example."
    },
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "change": "Add a 'Multi-Variant Consensus' subsection: run OCR on at least {default, autocontrast+PSM6, 2x-upscaled+PSM6} variants; for each variant compute (tier, value); pick the value that (a) comes from the highest-priority tier observed across variants, then (b) has the most variant votes, then (c) comes from the latest line. Provide the pick_best_total helper in the skill text."
    },
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "change": "Add a numeric sanity filter: reject any candidate total that is >10x the median of other same-tier candidates across variants, and reject totals outside (0.01, 1_000_000); on rejection fall back to the next candidate, and if none remain emit None."
    },
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "change": "Rewrite extract_date to: (1) first search only lines whose upper-cased text contains 'DATE', 'TARIKH', 'INV DATE', or 'INVOICE DATE' (and not 'PRINT DATE'/'CLOSE'); (2) only if none found, fall back to a full-text scan; (3) for ambiguous NN/NN/NNNN strings, parse as day-first by default and document the override hook; (4) clamp to a plausible year range (e.g., 2000-2099) and return None otherwise."
    },
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "change": "Add a 'Per-Image Budget' note: cap OCR variants to a small fixed set (3–5); on any exception or if all variants fail to produce a tiered match, return (None, None) rather than looping. State explicitly that null is the correct output when extraction is uncertain."
    },
    {
      "skill": "xlsx",
      "change": "In the Strict-Schema Outputs canonical pattern, add a final normalization step before to_excel: df = df.replace({'': None, 'nan': None, 'NaN': None, 'None': None}); df = df.where(pd.notna(df), None); and explicitly state 'Never write empty strings — they are indistinguishable from real values to some graders.'"
    },
    {
      "skill": "xlsx",
      "change": "Extend the post-write verification snippet to assert that cells expected to be null read back as NaN/None, e.g. assert check['results'].isna().sum().sum() == expected_null_count or at minimum assert no cell equals '' or the literal string 'nan'."
    },
    {
      "skill": "xlsx",
      "change": "In Pitfalls, add a bullet: 'Writing \"\" for a failed extraction — always coerce to None/pd.NA before to_excel so the cell is truly empty.'"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": {
    "overall": 0.78,
    "notes": "Four specific wrong fields across 22 receipts (reward 0.909) with identifiable per-receipt causes give high confidence in the pick-last-in-tier, multi-variant voting, label-anchored date, and null-coercion fixes. The 074 hallucination (702.00) is diagnosed indirectly from the image + predicted value since no raw OCR text is in this window; the voting+sanity-bound remedy generalizes beyond the specific token. Root-cause for 034 (date) is likely-but-not-certain label-proximity vs day-first parsing — both repairs are defensive and compatible."
  }
}
